# Autonomous skeletal reduction of USC-Mech II: quantitative accuracy/complexity trade-off

Principal investigator run, 2026-09-16.  All numbers below are produced by the
scripts in `src/` from the raw JSON inputs in `results/`, `cases/` and `mech/`.
Nothing in the parent mechanism was refitted: **every reduced mechanism is a
strict sub-set of the supplied parent (species deleted, and with them the
reactions that involve them, plus an optional reaction-only trimming pass)**.

## 0. Summary

* Parent: 111 species / 784 reactions (Cantera 3.2.0 reading of the supplied
  `parent.yaml`).
* Reduction targets macroscopic observables only: constant-volume adiabatic
  **ignition delay** and 1-D freely propagating **laminar flame speed**.
* Reduction criteria tested: DRGEP error propagation, flux participation,
  leave-one-out (LOO) observable sensitivity, and a **greedy observable-driven
  species add-back** search (the winner).
* Acceptance tolerances, fixed before the sweep and referenced to the parent
  mechanism: max |Δτ/τ| ≤ 30 % and max |Δs_L/s_L| ≤ 10 % over 401 cases, with
  **zero** cases that ignite/burn in the parent failing in the reduced
  mechanism.
* Results are summarised in §6 and §7.  The best mechanisms found and the
  mechanisms actually submitted are listed in §7: a **66-species /
  327-reaction** primary set (45 species and 457 reactions removed, −40.5 % /
  −58.3 % relative to the parent, worst case 28.6 % ignition and 6.9 % flame
  error, zero hard failures), a 73-species conservative set and a 60-species
  aggressive set.
* The reaction network can be cut much further than the species set: 135 of the
  462 reactions of the 66-species set (29 %) are individually inactive in every
  sampled state (activity ≤ 0.022 of the maximum reaction flux, §7.1) and their
  removal does not degrade any validated observable.
* Experimental validation: ignition against 185 hydrocarbon (set B) and 146
  usable H₂/O₂ (set A) shock-tube points, and flame speeds against the 70
  archive points of set D (benzene/CH₄/H₂, 1 atm, 7 datasets; set C is the
  φ-resolved benzene sub-set of the same measurements).  All of these conditions
  lie outside the 401-case design matrix, and the delivered primary mechanism
  stays inside both tolerances on the measured flame points too.
* Three independent negative/limiting results are reported honestly in §8:
  DRGEP collapses in this mechanism/case configuration, the smallest
  sub-40-species sets silently lose the equilibrium products, and the available
  public experimental data cannot discriminate the reduction in the H2/O2
  subset while the new hydrocarbon data sets (ignition and benzene/air flame
  speeds) do.

