3. **own estimates** — solver outputs (τ, s_L, equilibrium temperatures) computed
   in this run.

## 2. Methods

### 2.1 Observables

* **Ignition**: constant-volume, adiabatic, homogeneous reactor.
  `τ` = time of maximum dT/dt, obtained from the integrator trace with quadratic
  interpolation around the peak (integrator `rtol=1e-9`, `atol=1e-20`,
  `max_time_step=1e-3`).  A second definition, `τ_cross` = time at which T first
  exceeds T₀ + 400 K, is stored for every case as a consistency check.
  Numerical robustness: changing `rtol` from 1e-7 to 1e-11 moves τ by < 0.01 %
  (checked on the parent).
* **Flame**: laminar speed of a freely propagating 1-D flame, mixture-averaged
  transport, no Soret, grid refinement ratio/slope/curve = 4/0.3/0.5 with
  Cantera automatic re-gridding.  Converged grid sizes are 50–70 points.

Error metrics (parent = reference):
`e_ig = 10^(log10 τ_red − log10 τ_parent) − 1` and `e_fl = s_L,red/s_L,parent − 1`.
A case where the parent ignites but the reduced mechanism does not is counted as
a **hard failure** (`inf`) and reported separately, never averaged away.

### 2.2 Case matrix (401 parent cases)

* 10 fuels: H2, CH4, C2H4, C2H6, C3H8, n-C4H10, i-C4H10, C6H6, toluene,
  50/50 H2/CO syngas (all in "air", N2/O2 = 3.76).
* **Ignition (380)**: φ ∈ {0.5, 1, 2} × T ∈ {1000, 1250, 1600, 2000} K ×
  P ∈ {1, 10, 30} atm, plus 20 Ar-diluted shock-tube-style cases
  (φ ∈ {1,2}, P ∈ {1,10} atm, T = 1400 K).
* **Flames (21)**: 7 fuels (H2, CH4, C2H4, C2H6, C3H8, n-C4H10, syngas) ×
  φ ∈ {0.6, 1.0, 1.4}, 1 atm, 300 K.
* One parent case (`ig_CH4_phi2_T1000_P1`) does not ignite in the parent itself
  and is excluded from all error statistics (380→379 usable ignition cases).
* **Train / held-out split** (used only where a ranking criterion needs a
  sub-set): train = φ ∈ {1,2} ∧ T ∈ {1000,1600} K ∧ P ∈ {1,30} atm, the
  Ar-diluted cases, and the φ ∈ {1.0,1.4} flames (114 cases); held-out = φ = 0.5,
  T ∈ {1250,2000} K, P = 10 atm, φ = 0.6 flames.

