### 4.3 What the experimental comparison can and cannot show

Because all reduced mechanisms in this study retain the complete H2/O2 sub-set,
the **H2/O2 experimental comparison is essentially identical for parent and
reduced mechanisms** (median |Δlog10 τ| ≈ 1e-7 at 73 species): set A documents
the parent's absolute accuracy, not the reduction error.  Set B is the
discriminating experimental check and is reported for the delivered mechanisms.

