### 4.5 Set D (multi-fuel archive flame speeds, 70 points, 1 atm)

Set C covers one laboratory.  Extending the sweep to the whole archive gives 94
laminar-burning-velocity datasets, of which 73 contain a fuel of this study.
Among the points that otherwise pass the pressure/temperature/speed filters, 82
are ammonia-blended (NH₃ is not in USC-II) and most of the rest use He/Ar/CO₂
dilution.  Requiring 1 atm (0.9–1.1), T₀ = 280–420 K, a physical speed
(5–400 cm/s), O₂ plus a study fuel,
and **every species present in the parent mechanism**, leaves **70 points from 7
datasets** (H₂ 53, benzene 10, CH₄ 7; `cases/cases_flame_exp3.json`).  The
measured mole fractions are used verbatim as the unburnt mixture, so
oxygen-enriched and N₂-diluted cases are covered as measured (`src/lbv.py`,
job 7959143).

