Reading:

* The **delivered primary mechanism stays inside the 10 % flame tolerance on all
  70 measured points** (mean 2.2 %, worst 8.3 %) — and the worst points are the
  same benzene flames as in Set C.  The aggressive 60-species set exceeds the
  tolerance (up to 17 % on benzene), which is consistent with its role.
* The reduction error is *smallest* where the species set is untouched: H₂
  flames (53 points) agree with the parent to ≤ 4.6 % for every delivered
  mechanism, because the whole H₂/O₂ core is retained (§4.3).  The experimental
  discrimination comes from CH₄ (≤ 4.8 %) and benzene (≤ 8.3 %).
* **The absolute deviation from experiment is the parent's, not the reduction's.**
  The parent over-predicts heavily N₂-diluted lean H₂ flames by up to 47 % (its
  worst points), and the reduced mechanisms inherit that error almost unchanged.
  Part of it is physical-model error that no species reduction can address: the
  flame calculations use mixture-averaged transport without Soret, which is
  known to matter for H₂-rich flames, and the parent mechanism itself was not
  tuned to these diluted conditions.
* Numerical convergence: re-solving the three hardest cases with a finer grid
  (ratio 3 / slope 0.2 / curve 0.3, half the domain) moves s_L by 0.9–1.8 %,
  i.e. well below the deviations discussed here.

## 5. Verification of the reduced mechanisms

Checks performed for every candidate (`src/verify.py`,
`results/verify_all.json`, and `verify_final.json` for the delivered set):

Validation of the delivered set was done on the full 401-case matrix (not on the
search probe): `results/valf/val_final/` and `verify_final.json`.

**Independent re-execution of the delivered files.**  `final/lut50_g66.yaml`
(the same species set as the delivered primary file, full reaction list),
`final/lut60.yaml`, `final/lut40_g60.yaml` and `final/lut50_base.yaml` were
re-run locally (2-core node, same `src/runset.py`, fresh Cantera processes) on a
7-case sub-set that includes the binding worst case (`ig_C6H6_phi2_T2000_P30`)
and two flame cases, together with the parent (`results/local_check/`).  Every
local τ and s_L agrees with the 64-core run to ≤ 1e-4 % (floating-point
round-off), e.g. the 66-species set gives −28.59 % on the benzene worst case and
−8.73 % on `fl_C3H8_phi1.4`, exactly the values tabulated below.  The reported
trade-off therefore reflects the submitted files, not a transient intermediate
artifact.  The delivered primary file `final/lut50_t327.yaml` was produced and
validated entirely inside job 7958806 (401-case matrix + `verify_trim3.json` +
set-B run, driver `run_trim3.sh`); its YAML loads in a fresh Cantera 3.2.0
process with 66 species / 327 reactions and the same equilibrium temperatures as
the parent (2350.8 K for benzene/air φ = 1 here), and re-running three of its
cases locally (including the binding benzene worst case) reproduces the 64-core
τ to ≤ 1.1 × 10^-6 relative (`results/trim3_local/`).

| check | result |
|---|---|
| element balance of every reaction | max relative imbalance **0.0** (exactly balanced) for all sets |
| number of unbalanced reactions | **0** for all sets |
| thermo/transport of retained species vs parent | max difference **0.0** (identical NASA polynomials and transport fits) |
| HP-equilibrium T of 6 fuel/air mixtures | identical to parent (0.0 K) for every delivered mechanism (66, 73 and even 60 species); see below |

**Species floor from thermodynamics.**  Reduced sets are element-conserving by
construction, but below ≈ 40 species they no longer contain the equilibrium
products.  At 53–73 species ΔT_eq = 0.0 K; at 43–48 species ΔT_eq = 0.0 K; at
38 species (lut25) ΔT_eq = −402…−723 K; at 33 species (lut20, loo20) −402…−723 K;
at 27–31 species (flu20/flu25) −1203…−1849 K (H2/air φ = 1 equilibrium drops
from 2833 K to 985 K).  Consequently **no mechanism below ≈ 43 species is
recommended for any use**, even when its ignition/flame errors look tolerable:
it is no longer the same physical system.

